## The model

No component hard-codes a color; every visual reads a CSS custom property, so re-theming is a stylesheet change. The four layers run widest first. Pick the **narrowest** one that solves the problem.

| Layer | Where it lives | Scope |
|-------|----------------|-------|
| Global tokens | `:root` in `base.css` | Everything |
| Theme selectors | `[data-theme='dark']`, `[data-tx-contrast='high']` | A whole mode |
| BUI tokens | `--tx-bui-*` | The AI suite |
| Component hooks | `--tx-<component>-*` | One component, or one subtree |

The token inventory is in [Design Foundations](./foundations.en.mdc).

## Global tokens

Redefine tokens after importing `base.css`. Components resolve them at paint time, so an override applies to the whole subtree below it.

:::TuffCodeBlock{lang="css"}
---
code: |
  @import '@talex-touch/tuffex/base.css';

  :root {
    --tx-color-primary: #7c5cff;
    --tx-border-radius-base: 8px;
    --tx-transition-duration: 0.24s;
  }
---
:::

`--tx-color-primary-soft` and `--tx-coloring-border-color` are `color-mix()` expressions on `--tx-color-primary`, so they follow it. The primary ramp (`--tx-color-primary-light-*`, `--tx-color-primary-dark-2`) is fixed hex, and the default focus ring reads from it; override the ramp too when rebranding.

## Dark mode

Dark is a selector, not a media query: set `data-theme="dark"` or the `dark` class on any ancestor.

:::TuffCodeBlock{lang="html"}
---
code: |
  <html data-theme="dark">
  <!-- or -->
  <html class="dark">
---
:::

- The two are equivalent, so Tuffex drops into a Tailwind app (`.dark`) or a `data-theme` app without an adapter.
- Set either on a subtree to get a dark island on a light page.
- Dark takes each of the three emphasis weights 40 lighter to offset the irradiation that makes light text on a dark ground look bolder: `--tx-font-weight-medium` 500 → 460, `--tx-font-weight-semibold` 600 → 560, `--tx-font-weight-bold` 700 → 660; body text stays at 400. Your own styles follow by reading `var(--tx-font-weight-medium, 500)`. When overriding them, keep each dark value within (light − 100, light], or static fonts switch to another face; see [Retinal Irradiation & Weight Tuning](../concepts/irradiation-tuning.en.mdc).

### View Transitions

When toggling dark or light mode, Tuffex provides `applyThemeTransition`, a transition helper built on top of the native View Transitions API. The default preset is `circle-blur`, which expands outward from the pointer's click position using an SVG Gaussian-blurred mask for a soft, tactile glow.

Additional presets include `circle` (sharp circular clip), `polygon` (diagonal slash), `polygon-gradient` (gradient slash), `wipe` (horizontal wipe), `fade` (cross-fade), and custom GIF masks.

:::TuffDemoWrapper{demo="ThemingThemeTransitionDemo" code-lang="vue"}
---
code: |
  <script setup lang="ts">
  import { applyThemeTransition } from '@talex-touch/tuffex/utils'
  import { ref } from 'vue'

  const isDark = ref(false)

  function toggle(event: MouseEvent) {
    applyThemeTransition(() => {
      isDark.value = !isDark.value
      document.documentElement.classList.toggle('dark', isDark.value)
    }, {
      origin: event,
      variant: 'circle-blur',
      duration: 450,
      blurAmount: 3.5,
    })
  }
  </script>

  <template>
    <button @click="toggle">
      {{ isDark ? 'Light' : 'Dark' }}
    </button>
  </template>
---
:::

#### Presets and options

| Variant (`variant`) | Duration | Description |
|---------------------|----------|-------------|
| `circle-blur` (default) | 450ms | Expanding circular glow with SVG Gaussian blur originating at click position |
| `circle` | 350ms | Sharp circular clip-path expansion from click position |
| `polygon` | 600ms | Diagonal optical slash reveal |
| `polygon-gradient` | 800ms | Diagonal slash with linear gradient falloff |
| `wipe` | 400ms | Horizontal inset swipe |
| `fade` | 250ms | Smooth cross-fade transition |
| `circle-blur-top-left` | 600ms | Blurred circle originating from top-left corner |
| `gif` | 1500ms | Custom animated mask using `maskUrl` |

- **Origin resolution**: `origin` accepts a `MouseEvent`, `{ clientX, clientY }`, or `[x, y]`. Defaults to viewport center if omitted.
- **Accessibility**: Automatically falls back to immediate theme application when `prefers-reduced-motion` is active or if the browser lacks View Transition support.

## High contrast

A fourth palette that raises text and border contrast in light and dark.

| Trigger | Effect |
|---------|--------|
| `html[data-tx-contrast='high']` or `html.contrast` | On, explicitly |
| `@media (prefers-contrast: more)` | On, following the OS |
| `html[data-tx-contrast='normal']` | Opts **out** of the media query |

With `data-theme="dark"` and either high-contrast trigger, the dark high-contrast palette applies; the two themes don't stack.

### Materials

Under high contrast, components stop letting the page through:

| Part | Under high contrast |
|------|---------------------|
| Material panels: every `TxBaseSurface` mode but `plain` (Card, BaseAnchor panels, the command palette, the dialogs and the rest build on it; `plain` paints no material and gets no fill in high contrast either), GlassSurface, Toast, NavBar, TabBar, Picker, Slider, the RadioGroup indicator, the ProgressBar mask, StatCard, Drawer's transparent panel, MotionTransition's glass curtain | An opaque fill; no blur, no refraction, no rim light |
| Scrims: Modal, Drawer, BlowDialog | Keep their dimming, lose the frost |
| Layers over content: LoadingOverlay, the Card and DataTable loading veils, ImageUploader's remove button | Opaque, hiding what's under them |
| Decoration: FlowLight, the GlowText shine, GradualBlur | Hidden |

Light tints inside a component (hover, selected and input fills) are unchanged. The rule lives in the `tx-when-high-contrast` mixin in `style/mixins.scss`, which answers to the same triggers as the palette.

## AI suite tokens

`--tx-bui-*` came over with the Beautiful UI components (surface, inset, field, ink, and accent / green / orange / red / violet with matching tints) and has its own dark block under the same `[data-theme='dark']` / `.dark` selectors. Override it when AI surfaces shouldn't inherit your brand hue:

:::TuffCodeBlock{lang="css"}
---
code: |
  :root {
    --tx-bui-accent: #7c5cff;
    --tx-bui-accent-tint: #f0ecff;
  }
---
:::

## Component hooks

`--tx-<component>-*` restyles one component without touching the global palette. Names are predictable (`--tx-collapse-header-bg`, `--tx-avatar-ring-color`, `--tx-progress-height`), and each has a fallback. They inherit, so setting them on a wrapper themes that subtree only.

:::TuffCodeBlock{lang="vue"}
---
code: |
  <template>
    <section class="settings-panel">
      <TxCollapse v-model="open">
        <TxCollapseItem title="Appearance" name="appearance">…</TxCollapseItem>
      </TxCollapse>
    </section>
  </template>

  <style scoped>
  .settings-panel {
    --tx-collapse-radius: 6px;
    --tx-collapse-header-bg: transparent;
    --tx-collapse-border: rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.24);
  }
  </style>
---
:::

Each component page lists the hooks it reads. Use them instead of descendant selectors into component internals: custom properties are the supported surface, class names are not.

## Caveats

- When a component exposes a fill hook, set the token, not `background-color`: some fills are `background-image` gradients, and `background-color` paints behind them.
- Import `base.css` exactly once. With two copies, the one that loads last wins, which is rarely the one you edited.

## Technologies

- Tokens and theme selectors: `packages/tuffex/packages/components/style/variables.scss`.
- AI suite tokens: `packages/tuffex/packages/components/style/bui-tokens.scss`.
- Runtime entry: `@talex-touch/tuffex/base.css`.
